    {
      "reason": "Assess novelty and establish simpler controls that distinguish learned asymmetric relationships from transition-count memorization.",
      "query": "How do FPMC, TransRec, and sparse item-to-item sequential recommenders combine asymmetric transition scores with personalized sequential scores? Compare their formulations with a SASRec residual gated by distinct-user transition counts, including count-only baselines and popularity-normalized transition estimates."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve the strongest methodological risk: leave-user-out gating can eliminate singleton-edge training while enabling those edges at inference, and the loader lacks user IDs.",
      "query": "In sequential recommendation with sparse transition-count features, how do leave-one-user-out estimation and user-level cross-fitting prevent target leakage while controlling train-inference feature-distribution mismatch? Investigate treatment of singleton transitions, identity requirements, and direct-adjacent versus multi-step counts when scoring from the latest three items."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Determine whether the proposed implementation and validation can reliably isolate gains within the fixed budget.",
      "query": "What efficient PyTorch designs support batched sparse directed-edge count lookups and bounded candidate-specific residual scoring for SASRec, including chunked full-catalog inference? What paired uncertainty estimates and ablations are appropriate when comparing models on fixed sampled HR@10 with 200 users per category, 99 negatives, four categories, and repeated validation-based model selection?"
    }
  ]
